WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:04.375
Hey, welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:06.125
Do you remember our can roof?

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:13.541
So many of you were wondering
how it would sound with the rain, so here it is!

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.291
In this update we
will do 3 different things.

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:20.680
We will maintain the lagoon of our neighbors,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.708
we will work
a lot in our pig trailer and

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:26.083
we will do something
related with this toilet.

00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:28.458
Keep on watching if
you want to see what happens.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.791
But first, we´ll start by the laggon.

00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:34.458
In the beginning of the
season we cleared the lagoon area.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.833
We took all the mud out of the lagoon to

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:38.916
make it a nice
place to cool down in summer.

00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:43.875
It has served us very well, not
only for us but also for the plants.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.083
Now the summer is over and a lot of fast

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:49.791
growing plants sprouted
and took over the place again.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.791
These wild grapes are climbing the trees.

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:55.750
Even in the bottom
of the waterfall, where

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.333
the soil got
exposed to the sun, these kind

00:00:58.375 --> 00:00:59.833
of plants took over.

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:08.500
Also here, and in the pathways, and in
the terrace, our yellow gate got all dirty.

00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:12.375
And accessing the lagoon from
this side is not possible anymore.

00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:14.833
It is now a wall of cane.

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:20.416
And on top of that we also
lost a lot of water due to evaporation.

00:01:20.916 --> 00:01:22.083
That's where the water used to be!

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:25.208
We lost a lot like almost 20 centimeters.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.791
So let's start at the bottom.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.250
So today we're
going to start removing all

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.625
of these overgrown
vines, some leftover wood

00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:43.291
that is here and just
making this place a bit nicer.

00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:49.958
Debbie, what did you find?

00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:52.833
I found a huge tree!

00:01:53.125 --> 00:01:53.833
It is huge!

00:01:54.916 --> 00:01:57.416
It was actually a
super huge chestnut, it was dead.

00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:01.875
And Jaime cut it and made
this lovely bridge with chestnuts.

00:02:02.958 --> 00:02:03.458
Wow!

00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:21.583
As you can see, we
have now cleared this area.

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:26.875
And we are now going to
start clearing the area over there.

00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:34.500
The good thing is, you can take a
dip in the lagoon every 10 minutes or so.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.000
It's nice.

00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:41.291
Now it's time to remove this sketchy
dam that Dave built last year, sorry Dave.

00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:47.040
We are doing this because when we cleared the lagoon,

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.960
all the sand got stuck between the dam.

00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:52.791
To make this flow away in
winter, we are removing these rocks.

00:03:00.666 --> 00:03:02.000
One, two, three!

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:03.750
Nice!

00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:18.541
Are you done?

00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:19.041
Yeah.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.083
Done with the dam?

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.750
Obviously we wouldn't skip the
opportunity to clean the yellow gate.

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.791
As you can see, it got a bit dirty.

00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:30.958
Full of algae.

00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:39.791
We removed the dam, we cleaned
the door and also a bit the wall.

00:03:40.291 --> 00:03:43.791
Now it's a much nicer place to
enjoy and let the winter do its thing.

00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:49.083
So dangerous.

00:03:49.708 --> 00:03:51.666
So we already worked on the lower area.

00:03:51.916 --> 00:03:54.833
Now it's time to work on
the path to access the lagoon.

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:57.875
As you can see,
plants are growing all over.

00:03:57.875 --> 00:04:00.041
You have to walk around them, some are

00:04:00.041 --> 00:04:02.583
spiky, so it's way
better if you have all of this.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.500
Nice and clean, easy access for barefoot

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.333
people, for normal
people to get to the lagoon.

00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:34.250
What happened Doris?

00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:37.000
A thorn got stuck on my feet

00:04:39.375 --> 00:04:40.833
This is why we are doing this.

00:04:53.291 --> 00:04:56.208
A bit better now,
there is more room to go through.

00:04:56.708 --> 00:04:58.000
Because this rock was always in the way.

00:05:22.416 --> 00:05:22.916
Done.

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:44.666
So as you can see, it looks already much

00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:47.375
better, much
cleaner, way easier to access.

00:05:47.416 --> 00:05:48.708
Nice for the feet.

00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:52.500
So as you can see, this
part looks now much cleaner.

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:59.625
Now we have more areas to lay
down, to rest, it just looks much nicer.

00:06:06.166 --> 00:06:08.875
As you saw in the last lagoon update, we

00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:11.750
built these lovely
terraces here and we put inside

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.375
the soil that we took from the lagoon.

00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:16.333
It's really fertile soil
for the grass and everything that

00:06:16.333 --> 00:06:20.416
we want to plant, but it's
also really good for all of this.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.208
So today we are going
to clean all of this and plant

00:06:24.208 --> 00:06:27.375
some grass to slowly make
this into a nice grass terrace.

00:07:00.666 --> 00:07:01.375
It's done? 

00:07:02.291 --> 00:07:04.625
Yes, the things we can do
with the brushcutter are done.

00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:09.375
Now we have to go by hand and
remove the climmbing plants for the trees.

00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:12.541
Trees are being eaten alive by these...

00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:14.833
Yeah, they grow really fast.

00:07:15.625 --> 00:07:21.250
You can see it's slowly taking
over the tree, so I have to manage it a bit.

00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:26.916
That's what these plants do.

00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:29.958
They can really take over.

00:07:33.375 --> 00:07:38.375
You cannot pull because it's
stuck, so you have to unwind it a bit.

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:42.583
So as you can see, this
one had a little accident and it

00:07:42.583 --> 00:07:48.041
just broke down, probably a
disease or it was too weak here.

00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:51.875
But you can see already
some shoots here and also this

00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:57.375
one, so we can basically
chop off this one and let it grow up.

00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:10.500
So with the ones
that we chopped down from this

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.416
willow, we are going
to stake them into the ground.

00:08:13.958 --> 00:08:16.166
Hopefully they will grow new trees.

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:19.083
Ooh, deep.

00:08:19.458 --> 00:08:26.166
As deep as we can, we are putting them almost all in the same place.

00:08:26.916 --> 00:08:31.416
So we have more
probabilities of just adding new trees.

00:08:33.375 --> 00:08:33.875
So it's done.

00:08:34.916 --> 00:08:38.833
Hopefully next year
we'll have growing willows here.

00:08:39.583 --> 00:08:42.958
So we have already
cleared all this area and

00:08:42.958 --> 00:08:46.375
now we want to start
putting some grass patches.

00:08:46.375 --> 00:08:55.291
So we will prepare the soil a little
bit first, loose for this big patch of grass.

00:08:58.708 --> 00:09:03.958
So they have, hopefully
we'll have new grass patches.

00:09:04.541 --> 00:09:06.958
So now that we are
finished on this side, we

00:09:06.958 --> 00:09:09.041
are going to start
working on the other side.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.375
This is the other side, as
you can see, completely overgrown.

00:09:12.375 --> 00:09:16.083
You can barely see the
steps that we worked so hard to make.

00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:19.541
It's just time to brushcut
and show the beauty that it has.

00:09:20.083 --> 00:09:23.041
As it is now, we cannot
access the lagoon from this side.

00:09:23.458 --> 00:09:26.041
All of this cane
grew only within one year.

00:09:26.625 --> 00:09:28.166
I would say very invasive.

00:09:28.791 --> 00:09:30.666
And there are also many native trees in

00:09:30.666 --> 00:09:32.958
this area that are
almost covered by the cane.

00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:36.541
Currently we cannot even
reach the figs from the fig tree.

00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:39.000
Enough reason to take the cane out.

00:10:14.666 --> 00:10:17.458
So we have cleared
that side of the lagoon.

00:10:17.875 --> 00:10:21.375
We chopped all the canes that
were there, removed some of their roots.

00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:25.541
But the roots were
holding all the soil there.

00:10:26.041 --> 00:10:30.666
So we have here some
willow prunings that we did.

00:10:32.166 --> 00:10:37.166
So what we are going to do is
putting them on the soil horizontally.

00:10:38.375 --> 00:10:42.708
And hopefully we'll have a lot
of trees growing from just one stick.

00:10:44.041 --> 00:10:51.333
Some of the eyes where the shoots of
the trees will grow need to be facing upwards.

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:52.625
There are some here.

00:10:53.666 --> 00:10:58.625
So we can let them facing upwards.

00:10:59.916 --> 00:11:01.708
And we will just cover it.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:10.458
The likelihood of these two to
sprouts is still a little bit low.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.333
So we are staking as much as possible.

00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:17.166
And I'm also going to
put some of them vertically.

00:11:22.958 --> 00:11:24.000
So this patch is done.

00:11:24.916 --> 00:11:28.875
I'm going to do it on
the other side and also up top.

00:11:29.541 --> 00:11:33.458
So we have better ground support.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.208
And yeah, it's done for now.

00:11:47.458 --> 00:11:49.708
So before the
summer we cleared the lagoon.

00:11:50.083 --> 00:11:53.375
Most of the dirt that we
moved we built a lovely terrace there.

00:11:53.375 --> 00:11:56.375
But we also sent a lot of mud
and sand downstream down the waterfall.

00:11:56.375 --> 00:12:00.916
Most of the mud and sand that
came down got stuck between the rocks.

00:12:00.916 --> 00:12:02.375
Combined with the water and the heat and

00:12:02.375 --> 00:12:05.666
sand from the summer
made this huge jungle here.

00:12:06.166 --> 00:12:08.291
So now before the
winter comes and a lot of

00:12:08.291 --> 00:12:11.583
water will flow we are
going to help out the stream

00:12:11.583 --> 00:12:14.791
by cleaning this a bit and
make it look nice for the next season.

00:12:19.166 --> 00:12:19.666
Looking good!

00:12:50.125 --> 00:12:51.166
We are almost done.

00:13:10.375 --> 00:13:14.083
First we thought let's clean it by
hand but then we thought of something better.

00:13:14.291 --> 00:13:16.625
We had some rain
past week, actually a lot,

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.208
And the lagoon
filled up, we can do a big

00:13:19.208 --> 00:13:20.833
flushing operation to leave it shiny.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:25.375
And because this is such an important
and dramatic event we brought some fans and

00:13:25.416 --> 00:13:28.375
expectators to join the show.

00:13:34.291 --> 00:13:35.750
Coming, coming!

00:13:43.375 --> 00:13:47.000
It's like this, a bit more, a bit more.

00:14:23.375 --> 00:14:26.000
The first maintenance
job of the waterfall is done.

00:14:27.458 --> 00:14:29.500
Finding the balance
between taking and careing

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.500
is not an easy task
but we will get the hang of it.

00:14:33.166 --> 00:14:35.750
The place feels way
nicer and more easy to access.

00:14:44.916 --> 00:14:47.125
The first autumn
rains filled up the lagoon.

00:14:49.041 --> 00:14:52.666
So in these last hot days we can
spread the towels on the terrace again.

00:14:53.291 --> 00:14:55.791
All together ready for the winter season.

00:15:00.791 --> 00:15:06.416
So finally we have all the
materials for the roof to finish it.

00:15:06.625 --> 00:15:09.000
Because in case you
didn't know now we have this

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.333
funky looking trailer
laying around in our land.

00:15:11.375 --> 00:15:15.916
This used to be a pig
trailer, I know it's hard to believe now.

00:15:16.125 --> 00:15:20.541
Finally we have our pig trailer here
ready to be transformed into a new house.

00:15:20.791 --> 00:15:25.083
So we already built all
the structure, insulated and in the

00:15:25.083 --> 00:15:28.541
last video we covered in
these lovely colors as you can see.

00:15:29.458 --> 00:15:31.166
Now we are finishing the roof.

00:15:31.833 --> 00:15:35.333
So Colline and me are
gonna kill it and finish the roof.

00:15:36.416 --> 00:15:36.916
So let's go.

00:15:37.416 --> 00:15:41.458
We have this first layer
which is only the vapor barrier.

00:15:42.458 --> 00:15:47.166
With the rain here I just saw
one hole where the rain went through.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.000
So right now we're
gonna start with the roof.

00:15:51.166 --> 00:15:56.458
We're gonna make a frame all around
where we're gonna put the insulation in.

00:15:56.875 --> 00:16:01.125
And then we're gonna
put a tarp over it and over

00:16:01.125 --> 00:16:04.375
that we're gonna place
the battens and then the roof.

00:16:04.375 --> 00:16:08.500
So right now we're
gonna install the frame first.

00:16:27.958 --> 00:16:29.333
We're gonna put the last beam.

00:16:31.416 --> 00:16:34.041
And you're gonna
put the most beautiful one.

00:16:34.458 --> 00:16:35.833
Yes, it's all broken.

00:16:36.375 --> 00:16:38.791
It's all broken.

00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:43.458
Done.

00:16:54.916 --> 00:16:56.291
Okay, so we have the whole frame in.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:02.000
So right now what we're gonna do is
put all the insulation in between those spaces.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:06.125
It's gonna be two layers
but we first have to cut some

00:17:06.125 --> 00:17:10.375
little pieces because it's
just a bit bigger than two sheets.

00:17:10.416 --> 00:17:16.500
Just on this side where it's
shadow you can see it's still a bit wet.

00:17:17.208 --> 00:17:20.250
So yeah, 20 minutes will be dry and then

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.375
we can start
putting all the insulation in.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.875
Okay, good stuff.

00:17:54.041 --> 00:17:59.708
I'm gonna put the last piece
so I can say to my mom that I helped.

00:18:01.208 --> 00:18:02.000
Good materials.

00:18:03.375 --> 00:18:08.500
Yeah, I need to not be allergic to
dust, but like it's better than my bed.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.916
If you are looking for a
hard worker, there you have it.

00:18:14.166 --> 00:18:14.833
Hire me.

00:18:15.458 --> 00:18:16.416
So the insulation is done.

00:18:17.791 --> 00:18:22.291
Right now we're gonna start
putting the tarp on for the waterproof layer.

00:18:23.583 --> 00:18:26.250
Yeah, we use this material.

00:18:27.125 --> 00:18:29.541
It's 80% recycled textile.

00:18:31.375 --> 00:18:36.333
Yeah, it's just a lot of fabric
turned apart and compressed together.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:41.666
I think it's gonna work. We'll
see if it's a good insulation or not.

00:18:42.375 --> 00:18:44.416
New material that we're trying out.

00:18:44.708 --> 00:18:49.458
As we mentioned before, this
insulation cannot get water in, which is a bit of a

00:18:49.458 --> 00:18:53.000
bummer because it requires
all these extra plastic layers.

00:18:55.791 --> 00:18:56.291
Pretty far.

00:19:02.791 --> 00:19:07.791
This one is to prevent the water
from getting in, but it lets humidity get out.

00:19:43.375 --> 00:19:47.083
Next layer are this
batten to hold the foil.

00:19:47.083 --> 00:19:50.208
And after to mount the roof sheets on
top.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.583
So we finished the tarp and all the battens.

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:08.250
We taped off all
the screws on the battens.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.625
And yeah, right now we're
gonna start putting the final roof in.

00:20:14.625 --> 00:20:17.541
So for the roof of
our house, we're gonna choose

00:20:17.541 --> 00:20:21.375
this corrugatal metal
sheet with insulation on it.

00:20:21.833 --> 00:20:26.375
We're gonna cut them, bring them in
the pickup, put them on top of our house.

00:20:27.375 --> 00:20:29.666
It's very light, very light.

00:20:30.333 --> 00:20:32.875
We thought we were there
to get second hand sheets, but

00:20:32.875 --> 00:20:35.500
actually they are just
the leftovers from the factory.

00:20:36.458 --> 00:20:39.041
As they are not in
perfect condition, people

00:20:39.041 --> 00:20:42.375
usually don't buy
them, but they still work for us.

00:20:57.375 --> 00:21:00.416
This is a bit noisy, a bit disgusting.

00:21:21.625 --> 00:21:22.125
Okay.

00:21:23.916 --> 00:21:24.583
You have it?

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:25.750
All you. All you.

00:21:52.708 --> 00:21:56.000
Yeah, this is the only shot we
have from the assembling of the roof.

00:21:56.666 --> 00:21:59.833
A bit shaky, but you can see everything.

00:22:04.541 --> 00:22:06.083
A little millimeter to me.

00:22:06.375 --> 00:22:06.875
Okay, wait.

00:22:08.708 --> 00:22:09.916
That's already good.

00:22:15.916 --> 00:22:16.458
Last sheet.

00:22:24.416 --> 00:22:26.000
Last sheet in place.

00:22:26.708 --> 00:22:29.791
I just gotta mark
now where the screws go.

00:22:31.208 --> 00:22:33.375
And I will start
drilling and putting the screws in.

00:23:10.625 --> 00:23:11.708
Okay, so the roof is in.

00:23:12.375 --> 00:23:14.916
Right now we're
gonna put the finished piece.

00:23:15.625 --> 00:23:18.875
It's to cover the
exposed foam in the front and in

00:23:18.875 --> 00:23:20.916
the back, but in the
back we have another piece here.

00:23:21.833 --> 00:23:25.333
Which also prevents the
rain from coming under the battens.

00:23:25.958 --> 00:23:29.375
First we're gonna install the
front and then we will install the big piece.

00:23:51.375 --> 00:23:53.500
Okay, we're almost done with the roof.

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:55.791
We only need the
siding to be done because

00:23:55.791 --> 00:23:58.291
we still see a bit of the anti-rain tarp.

00:23:59.125 --> 00:24:01.708
So what we're gonna do is
we're gonna put some wood in there.

00:24:02.125 --> 00:24:04.291
And sometime at kamp we don't have the

00:24:04.291 --> 00:24:06.333
right tools for the
things that we want to do.

00:24:06.625 --> 00:24:08.875
For example, here we
don't have a table saw yet.

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:13.333
So Julien made
this little guide handmade.

00:24:14.083 --> 00:24:15.208
It will do for now.

00:24:15.208 --> 00:24:19.125
It's not the official version,
but it suits for what we want to do.

00:24:19.375 --> 00:24:22.708
And we can just saw all day long.

00:24:40.375 --> 00:24:44.041
First we fix the battens on the
edges to screw the final pieces on top.

00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:50.041
Then we cover the foil
and screw our last wood layer.

00:24:52.958 --> 00:24:53.916
All around the trailer.

00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:10.166
Okay, we're almost done with the roof.

00:25:10.458 --> 00:25:12.125
But we still have one part to do.

00:25:12.375 --> 00:25:14.333
We're a bit running out
of wood because all of the wood

00:25:14.333 --> 00:25:18.666
that we're using is the
second hand not used from the sawmill.

00:25:19.416 --> 00:25:21.458
So our quantities are limited.

00:25:22.291 --> 00:25:24.041
So we're taking one
of these beams and instead

00:25:24.041 --> 00:25:27.500
of using the length,
we're gonna use the width.

00:25:28.458 --> 00:25:31.541
So I don't know how it's called in
English, but in French we call it "bardo".

00:25:32.375 --> 00:25:35.541
It's to cut the reins
of the wood in this direction.

00:25:36.125 --> 00:25:39.208
So we're cutting a bunch of
them and we're putting them together.

00:25:39.416 --> 00:25:41.250
This way we can save
a bit of wood every time.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.500
And that's what we
thought was the best for this one.

00:25:45.125 --> 00:25:45.958
Let's see how it goes.

00:26:42.375 --> 00:26:46.875
Okay, not perfect. Cool.

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:57.041
Okay, we're done
with the top part of the roof.

00:26:57.500 --> 00:27:00.500
So that means that we are
completely done with the outside of the trailer.

00:27:00.875 --> 00:27:02.291
Now we can focus more on the inside.

00:27:03.208 --> 00:27:07.375
So you see with all of this that we
did on the outside, we have many left over.

00:27:07.416 --> 00:27:09.958
The small ones are
gonna go for the pizza oven

00:27:09.958 --> 00:27:13.541
as firewood and the
big one we will reuse later.

00:27:13.916 --> 00:27:15.333
Maybe for inside middle wall.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:17.583
Everything outside
of the trailer is done.

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:19.166
Now we focus on the inside.

00:27:19.583 --> 00:27:20.250
It's very exciting.

00:27:20.708 --> 00:27:23.250
It's the end of the day
and Julien and I are gonna go eat.

00:27:24.250 --> 00:27:25.000
Stay tuned.

00:27:28.458 --> 00:27:30.083
So we're heading to the sawmill again.

00:27:31.083 --> 00:27:32.833
Yep, we are back in the sawmill.

00:27:33.583 --> 00:27:36.375
This time to get the wood
for the walls of the pig trailer.

00:27:36.375 --> 00:27:41.333
And of course we are gonna use
our beloved basketball court field.

00:27:44.791 --> 00:27:47.708
This time we asked them to
remove the top layer with a planer.

00:27:48.041 --> 00:27:50.708
To have a bit of color
variation inside the trailer

00:27:50.708 --> 00:27:53.708
and to save us from
sanding the entire thing by hand.

00:27:54.916 --> 00:27:56.833
Easy for them, easy for us.

00:28:04.708 --> 00:28:07.000
Maybe the other way, yeah.

00:28:15.375 --> 00:28:19.208
It's time now to focus on the
inside and to do the paneling of the wall.

00:28:19.500 --> 00:28:21.916
Which is the last step for the walls.

00:28:22.666 --> 00:28:26.958
We have here the same wood that
we used for the roof and the ground.

00:28:27.416 --> 00:28:29.000
It's the basketball court wood.

00:28:29.583 --> 00:28:30.083
Let's do it.

00:29:12.041 --> 00:29:14.666
Since the wood is
second hand, it has already

00:29:14.666 --> 00:29:18.750
been glued before
when it was a basketball field.

00:29:19.208 --> 00:29:22.416
So we are working with
the materials that have some time

00:29:22.416 --> 00:29:25.541
residue of some type of
glue, silicone, we already know.

00:29:26.083 --> 00:29:29.000
But that means that sometime we
have to take an extra time to clean it.

00:29:30.375 --> 00:29:35.291
This is a piece
98.6 and it goes right there.

00:30:37.208 --> 00:30:39.875
Ah, finally done with the paneling!

00:30:40.375 --> 00:30:44.666
It's all finished. We
only have some slight finishing to

00:30:44.666 --> 00:30:47.375
do, especially on the
edges of the windows and the door.

00:30:47.416 --> 00:30:52.250
Overall, it was very
long. It took us, I think, 8? No.

00:30:53.083 --> 00:30:55.791
6 days to do
everything and we were 2 people.

00:30:56.541 --> 00:31:00.125
So it was really long, but very
satisfying also, especially when it works.

00:31:00.666 --> 00:31:02.000
Sometimes it doesn't
work, sometimes it works.

00:31:03.291 --> 00:31:08.000
So yeah, finishing on the door
and the window and I think we're done.

00:31:08.625 --> 00:31:11.875
And we can move on to the
next steps to make this a proper house.

00:31:12.583 --> 00:31:13.083
Exciting!

00:31:17.791 --> 00:31:22.166
The outside of our level 2 house is
finally finished. Let us know what you think.

00:31:22.916 --> 00:31:24.583
And the inside is looking great.

00:31:25.583 --> 00:31:28.000
There are still
some small things to do, such

00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:30.458
as the sockets and
switches, install a stove...

00:31:30.791 --> 00:31:32.208
Watch out for spoilers!

00:31:33.708 --> 00:31:35.375
But that's for the next video.

00:31:35.833 --> 00:31:39.500
Because now Alize is gonna do
something very cool for this toilet.

00:31:44.083 --> 00:31:47.666
So this is the new compost toilet
we have been using for a couple of months.

00:31:48.041 --> 00:31:50.000
Everything is
perfect, just sometimes we can't

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:53.208
really tell if there's
somebody using the toilet or not.

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:54.500
No!

00:31:56.250 --> 00:32:00.541
So we think it would be a nice idea to
have a sign here to show the toilet vacancy.

00:32:06.166 --> 00:32:06.666
Sorry!

00:32:08.666 --> 00:32:11.666
So the idea is to
add a rotatable sign out on

00:32:11.666 --> 00:32:14.375
the door, which is
connected with the indoor lock.

00:32:14.791 --> 00:32:18.458
So every time when people lock
the door, the sign will turn into in use.

00:32:19.083 --> 00:32:21.083
We'll make it into a little bird shape as

00:32:21.083 --> 00:32:23.708
there is a lot of
birds living here around us.

00:32:24.375 --> 00:32:29.333
We have been clearing mimosa trees
beside the road for the fire resilience purpose.

00:32:29.958 --> 00:32:32.375
So we got a lot of mimosa wood here.

00:32:32.791 --> 00:32:34.083
Let's pick some for the door lock.

00:32:41.375 --> 00:32:44.458
So we have collected
some wood branches and we'll

00:32:44.458 --> 00:32:47.833
start making the indoor
lock with these pieces of wood.

00:32:54.583 --> 00:32:58.375
Now I'm using these tools to
create a flat surface on the wood branch.

00:33:06.166 --> 00:33:11.000
So now we have a nice flat surface here.

00:33:18.375 --> 00:33:22.375
Now we will apply some linseed oil
on the wood surface to protect the wood.

00:33:36.458 --> 00:33:39.375
Now we are finish
with the indoor handle.

00:33:40.791 --> 00:33:46.041
After finishing with the handle, I'm
making a draft of the little bird here on a

00:33:46.041 --> 00:33:49.375
cardboard to see if the size
is a good fit on the actual door.

00:33:59.375 --> 00:34:06.833
So now let's place the paper cut
bird here to see if the size fits or not.

00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:09.375
I think the size is okay.

00:34:33.875 --> 00:34:37.625
So here is a prototype of
how the lock is going to work.

00:34:38.291 --> 00:34:41.625
So when the door is
unlocked, the bird will stand like this.

00:34:42.125 --> 00:34:45.416
When we lock the
door inside, the bird will

00:34:45.416 --> 00:34:47.375
turn down like
eating some seed on the ground.

00:35:26.666 --> 00:35:28.666
So the bird lock is finished.

00:35:28.666 --> 00:35:30.458
Let´s see how people use it.

00:35:51.958 --> 00:35:54.208
Gui came on.

00:35:55.583 --> 00:35:56.625
You can go.

00:35:58.083 --> 00:35:59.750
It works.

00:36:02.958 --> 00:36:03.541
Cool.

